  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lao PDR Strengthening Education Ministry Capacity to Monitor and Evaluate Sectoral Programs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity will assist the Lao MOE design and build a results-based monitoring and evaluation (M&amp;E) system that will equip it to move more effectively towards a sector-wide approach to policy and program development.  Recognizing its commitments to the EFA and MDG agendas, as well as its continued relationship with donors, the MOE has created a Project Coordination Division (PCD) and the Policy Analysis Division (PAD). The PCD will be the institutional home for project-related M&amp;E activities, as well as a knowledge management center for learning gained through project implementation in the sector.  The MOE&apos;s long-term concerns are to extend its technical evaluation skills to cover all ODA-supported projects. With this grant, the MOE will design and build an M&amp;E system through a program that combines formal training workshops, guiding/mentoring, and hands-on M&amp;E activities.  A small consultant team will work alongside staff in situ, providing guidance in developing a number of M&amp;E systems, tools and products.  The consultants will accompany the MOE, as an institution, but will not substitute for it.  As staff knowledge and skills increase, they take on more complex tasks, with the consultants&apos; support moving from guidance to mentoring. While requiring more time than the &apos;substitution&apos; approach, this &apos;accompanying&apos; approach is likely to result in a more effective development of knowledge and skills.</narrative>
  </description>
